<Layout title="About" description="Brian Amadio: software engineer in Melbourne, formerly Cecil Earth, Myst AI and Stitch Fix.">
	<p>
		I'm a software engineer based in Melbourne with 9+ years building data platforms, forecasting
		systems and experimentation infrastructure.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Cecil Earth</strong> (2023–2026): one of three founding engineers. Designed the
			event-driven AWS platform serving 30+ geospatial datasets and the Cecil Python SDK.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Myst AI</strong> (2021–2022): renewable-energy forecasting platform architecture.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Stitch Fix</strong> (2018–2021): experimentation platform at ~1,000 req/s and 15 ms
			p99; author of <a href="https://github.com/stitchfix/mab">mab</a>; O'Reilly AI Superstream
			speaker (2021).
		</li>
		<li>
			PhD in experimental particle physics, UC Berkeley (ATLAS at the LHC). Shared the 2025
			Breakthrough Prize in Fundamental Physics with the ATLAS collaboration.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		<a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> · <a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a>
	</p>
